{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "thepghub.com/review-attempt",
  "version": 1,
  "minEngine": 2,
  "name": "Review my attempt",
  "description": "Reads the problem and the code in your PG.Hub editor and reviews what you actually wrote: complexity, correctness and whether a better approach exists. Asks for anything it cannot read.",
  "author": "you",
  "domains": [
    "thepghub.com"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "code",
    "complexity",
    "review"
  ],
  "match": {
    "pathRegex": "^/category/[^/]+/[^/]+",
    "hint": "Open a PG.Hub problem workspace. Anywhere else, paste the problem and your code in below."
  },
  "inputs": [
    {
      "key": "depth",
      "label": "Answer style",
      "type": "select",
      "default": "brief",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "brief",
          "label": "Brief - complexity and the one thing to fix"
        },
        {
          "value": "detailed",
          "label": "Detailed - walk through my code"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variables": {
    "slug": {
      "hidden": true,
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "url",
          "regex": "/category/[^/]+/([a-z0-9-]+)"
        }
      ],
      "transform": "slugToTitle"
    },
    "topic": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "url",
          "regex": "/category/([a-z0-9-]+)"
        },
        {
          "from": "literal",
          "value": "unknown"
        }
      ],
      "transform": "slugToTitle"
    },
    "title": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": "h1.ws-q-title"
        },
        {
          "from": "var",
          "name": "slug"
        }
      ],
      "maxChars": 200,
      "fallback": {
        "label": "Problem title",
        "type": "text",
        "placeholder": "Connected Components in an Undirected Graph"
      }
    },
    "difficulty": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-diff-badge"
        },
        {
          "from": "literal",
          "value": "not shown"
        }
      ],
      "maxChars": 40
    },
    "statement": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-q-desc"
        },
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-question"
        },
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-left-content"
        }
      ],
      "transform": "htmlToText",
      "maxChars": 6000,
      "fallback": {
        "label": "Problem statement",
        "type": "textarea",
        "rows": 6,
        "placeholder": "Paste the statement",
        "hint": "Only the open tab is in the page, so switch to Description, or select the text and press Use selection."
      }
    },
    "examples": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-examples"
        },
        {
          "from": "literal",
          "value": "(none shown on this page)"
        }
      ],
      "transform": "htmlToText",
      "maxChars": 3000
    },
    "constraints": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-constraints"
        },
        {
          "from": "literal",
          "value": "(none shown on this page)"
        }
      ],
      "transform": "htmlToText",
      "maxChars": 1500
    },
    "code": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".monaco-editor .view-lines"
        },
        {
          "from": "css",
          "selector": ".ws-editor-area pre"
        }
      ],
      "transform": "stripLineNumbers",
      "maxChars": 8000,
      "fallback": {
        "label": "Your code",
        "type": "textarea",
        "rows": 12,
        "placeholder": "Paste your solution",
        "hint": "The editor only keeps the visible lines in the page, so long files read short. Select all in the editor and copy, or press Use selection."
      }
    },
    "style": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "from": "input",
          "name": "depth"
        }
      ],
      "map": {
        "brief": "Give the time and space complexity in two lines, then the single most important thing to fix or improve.",
        "detailed": "Walk through the code: the loops, the data structures and the invariants. Then give the time and space complexity, and say whether a better bound is reachable."
      }
    }
  },
  "text": [
    "I am working on a programming problem and I want you to review the code I have written for it.",
    "",
    "### PROBLEM",
    "{{title}} — {{topic}}, level: {{difficulty}}",
    "",
    "{{statement}}",
    "",
    "### WORKED EXAMPLES",
    "{{examples}}",
    "",
    "### CONSTRAINTS",
    "{{constraints}}",
    "",
    "### MY CODE",
    "{{code}}",
    "",
    "### WHAT I WANT",
    "{{style}}",
    "",
    "This is my own code as it stands in my editor, not a model answer. Work with it: tell me what is wrong with THIS, rather than replacing it with a textbook solution, unless I ask for a different approach. If it is already correct and optimal, say so plainly instead of inventing something to change."
  ]
}
